@kamil.kreiser — the severity question, answered from S's code at develop `2c1d179` (`CardanoAnchorService.PerVerb.cs`, `CertifyAsync`):

**S never calls `POST /api/certifications/issue` without a holder.** The body is always `{ type: "signed_document", holderEmail, data: { note, contentHash }, parentDocumentId }`; `holderEmail` is derived from the acting person's address, and **when no email resolves S does not call the route at all** — it logs "certify tx … has no resolvable holder email; using /api/anchors fallback" and anchors flat. S never sends `holderId`.

So for S this path is **latent, not live**: every S certify takes the `holderEmail` branch and the `/api/users/stub` resolution, never the `holderId = issuer.id` default. Re-rate as you see fit (Low from S's side); the mis-attribution class still matters for any other connector.
